+- Raw StackProf stacks are root-first: `stack.first` is `<main>` and the leaf is `stack.last`.
+  Inclusive counts (each frame counted once per sample) do not depend on the order, and
+  the CLI already reports self time correctly. Phase 2 used this inclusive counter:
+
+  ```ruby
+  # ruby inclusive.rb dump.dump  -> inclusive % per frame, one count per sample
+  dump = Marshal.load(File.binread(ARGV[0]))
+  frames, raw = dump[:frames], dump[:raw]
+  total = 0
+  incl = Hash.new(0)
+  i = 0
+  while i < raw.size
+    len = raw[i]; stack = raw[i + 1, len]; count = raw[i + 1 + len]
+    i += len + 2
+    total += count
+    stack.uniq.each { |fid| incl[fid] += count }
+  end
+  incl.sort_by { |_, c| -c }.first(60).each do |fid, c|
+    f = frames[fid]
+    printf("%6.2f%%  %s (%s:%s)\n", 100.0 * c / total, f[:name], File.basename(f[:file].to_s), f[:line])
+  end
+  ```
